==English==

===Etymology===
From {{w|William Horlick}}, founder. Term extended as euphemism for {{term|bollocks||mess|lang=en}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{context|chiefly|British}} a [[malted]] [[milk]] [[hot]] [[bedtime]] [[drink]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=Horlicks}}

# {{context|euphemistic|chiefly|UK|slang}} [[bollocks]] – a [[muddle]], [[hash]] or [[balls-up]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb|Horlicks|es}}

# {{context|euphemistic|chiefly|UK|slang}} to make a hash (of something); to make a Horlicks of.

